  "configuration_id": "config_004",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_003: multimodal, singleprofile, scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, concat → acc 0.435), the single most important uncertainty is whether the image modality actually contributes meaningful signal or whether a simpler RNA-only model is competitive. config_004 (rna_only, singleprofile, scgpt, no aggregation, no fusion) is a clean single-variable ablation of config_003: the only difference is the removal of the image encoder and concat fusion, while keeping the same RNA encoder (scgpt), profile setting (singleprofile), and no aggregation. If config_004 matches or exceeds config_003, the image modality is not adding value and the search should pivot toward RNA-encoder and profile-setting choices. If config_003 is clearly better, multimodal fusion is justified and we can invest subsequent experiments in optimizing encoder choices, aggregation, and fusion strategy. This is the highest-information experiment under a tight budget because the answer reshapes the entire remaining search direction, and it changes exactly one design axis relative to the only data point we have."
}

